WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.868
Maya's car has broken down, and she needs two thousand dollars to fix it.

2
00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:06.353
Her credit file is thin.

3
00:00:06.353 --> 00:00:09.571
Her income and her bank account tell a better story.

4
00:00:10.422 --> 00:00:11.815
Maya has a pod.

5
00:00:11.815 --> 00:00:12.930
It is empty.

6
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.750
An identity service checks who she is, once, and gives her a credential.

7
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.363
Her employer's payroll provider states her income.

8
00:00:21.363 --> 00:00:26.280
This is the same application you saw in the mortgage demo, issuing to a different person.

9
00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:32.485
Her bank summarises her account: regular deposits, and no returned payments in ninety days.

10
00:00:33.335 --> 00:00:38.638
And the credit bureau adds its view: a score of six hundred and twelve, from a short history.

11
00:00:39.488 --> 00:00:41.663
Maya asks two lenders for a quote.

12
00:00:41.663 --> 00:00:45.052
Each receives a proof that she clears its thresholds.

13
00:00:45.052 --> 00:00:48.762
Neither receives her name, her income or her transactions.

14
00:00:49.612 --> 00:00:51.159
She picks one and applies.

15
00:00:51.159 --> 00:00:59.016
The lender is granted her identity, income and cash-flow records for thirty days, and the consent is recorded before the first read.

16
00:00:59.865 --> 00:01:02.471
The lender shows both ways of deciding.

17
00:01:02.471 --> 00:01:05.343
On the credit score alone, she is declined.

18
00:01:05.343 --> 00:01:08.016
With cash flow as well, she is approved.

19
00:01:08.867 --> 00:01:11.601
The loan disclosure is written to her pod.

20
00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:12.837
It is hers to keep.

21
00:01:13.687 --> 00:01:18.859
The bank that looked only at the score sends its decline, with reasons, to the same place.

22
00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:22.639
A payment service sends the money to her card.

23
00:01:22.639 --> 00:01:25.505
It is granted one record, once: where to pay.

24
00:01:25.505 --> 00:01:26.842
It sees nothing else.

25
00:01:27.692 --> 00:01:33.862
Each payment made on time is added to a repayment credential in her pod, and reported to the bureau.

26
00:01:33.862 --> 00:01:35.528
The thin file gets thicker.

27
00:01:36.378 --> 00:01:39.826
When the loan is paid off, Maya withdraws the lender's access.

28
00:01:40.676 --> 00:01:44.307
The lender asks for her bank data again, and the pod refuses.

29
00:01:45.197 --> 00:01:48.146
Five issuers, two lenders, one payment service.

30
00:01:48.146 --> 00:01:52.224
The next time Maya applies for anything, the pod is already full.

31
00:01:53.073 --> 00:01:58.663
Try it from the welcome page, or join us at the EDMA Solid Community of Practice.
